{"id":"u-c27ca0c5-7585-4a14-a077-658c7e342005","src":"community","title":"Power & Build 3","author":"Cedric Hamelryck","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/dvwSdP-power-and-build-3","desc":"Power & Build 3 is designed for lifters who want to build strength and muscle without turning every workout into a recovery challenge.\n\nThe program combines the best of two worlds: focused strength work on the major compound lifts and controlled, moderate-rep hypertrophy training for muscle growth.\n\nEach workout starts with one main strength lift — squat, bench press or deadlift — performed for 3×3 at approximately RPE 8. This keeps heavy lifting and strength progression at the core of the program without accumulating the fatigue that can come from performing multiple heavy compounds in the same session.\n\nThe remainder of each workout focuses primarily on stable machine and supported exercises in the 8–12 rep range at approximately RPE 8. The goal isn't simply to move as much weight as possible. Reps should be performed through a full range of motion, with minimal momentum, a controlled eccentric and a strong but controlled concentric.\n\nProgression is simple. On hypertrophy exercises, gradually add reps until you can perform 3×12 with good technique at approximately RPE 8. Then increase the weight and build back up from around 8 reps. On the main 3×3 lifts, increase the load gradually whenever all three sets remain technically clean and around the target RPE.\n\nThe underlying philosophy is stimulus over exhaustion. More fatigue does not automatically mean more progress. Training should provide enough stimulus to become stronger and more muscular while leaving enough recovery capacity to perform consistently week after week.\n\nYou don't need to crawl out of the gym for a workout to be productive. Train hard, move well, progress gradually, recover, and repeat.\n\n3 days per week. Full body. One heavy lift per session. Strength + hypertrophy. Sustainable progression.","l